1. REFINEMENT:
I keep the multi-start greedy + lexicographic local search structure, but squeeze more quality by:
- Increasing randomized restarts (40 → 120) with a time-budget guard so execution time stays bounded.
- Adding a perturbation phase: from the best placement found so far, randomly relocate a few models and re-run local search (an iterated local search), which often escapes local optima that pure restarts miss.
- Keeping the lexicographic (sorted-profile) objective for tie-breaking so the second-highest GPU KVPR is also reduced, improving robustness.

